<Rung Number="21" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
OUTPUT INITIALIZATION VALUES
============================================================
If CV1 is NOT being initialized, or if its initialization does not use the
Kp * E Offset function, copy the selected CV to the CV1 Initialization value.

If CV IS being initialized, AND the Offset function is being use,
and the primary's Proportional Gain is > 0.0,
we need to calculate a uni-directional offset to force
Primary #1 to have its error (difference between SP and PV)
change sign to be selected.
The offset pushes the CV1 primary away from being
selected (only), but only if its error sign is such that it will
not want to take control.

Note that the Error (Inp_E1) sign is based on the Control Action
configured in the PIDE, so we don't need to configure control action.
We just need to know whether this is a High-Select or a Low-Select
to know which direction to offset.

IMPORTANT:  Inp_Kp1 should come from the PIDE "PGain" parameter
and Inp_E1 should come from the PIDE "EPercent" parameter!

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added limiting of CVPrev to within Cfg_CVMin to Cfg_CVMax.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Out_UseCV1Prev) XIC(Cfg_CV1Offset) GRT(Inp_Kp1,0.0) [MUL(Inp_Kp1,Inp_E1,Wrk_CV1Offset) ,XIO(Cfg_HiLoSel) [GRT(Wrk_CV1Offset,0.0) ADD(Wrk_CV,Wrk_CV1Offset,Out_CV1Prev) ,LES(Wrk_CV1Offset,0.0) MOV(Wrk_CV,Out_CV1Prev) ] ,XIC(Cfg_HiLoSel) [LES(Wrk_CV1Offset,0.0) ADD(Wrk_CV,Wrk_CV1Offset,Out_CV1Prev) ,GRT(Wrk_CV1Offset,0.0) MOV(Wrk_CV,Out_CV1Prev) ] ] ,[XIO(Out_UseCV1Prev) ,XIO(Cfg_CV1Offset) ,LEQ(Inp_Kp1,0.0) ] MOV(Wrk_CV,Out_CV1Prev) ,LES(Out_CV1Prev,Cfg_CVMin) MOV(Cfg_CVMin,Out_CV1Prev) ,GRT(Out_CV1Prev,Cfg_CVMax) MOV(Cfg_CVMax,Out_CV1Prev) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
